        <p>See a clinician if the pain travels down your leg below the knee with numbness, tingling, or weakness; if it followed a fall or heavy impact rather than a lift; or if it is getting worse after a couple of weeks instead of better. And if you wake up locked up every day after training, <a href="/guides/morning-back-stiffness">the morning stiffness guide</a> covers what is normal and what is not.</p>

