        <p>Doing thirty easy glute bridges is less useful than moving on to a harder version. A simple ladder looks like this: clamshell, then glute bridge, then single-leg bridge. For stability work, short holds of around eight to ten seconds, repeated, tend to work better than one long shaky hold.</p>
